 ## Bound the work, not the archive
 
-Large collections should not require processing everything at once. *Bounded work* handles a limited portion at a time; a page of results does not limit the total number of results. Long operations progress through bounded steps that can resume after interruption.
+Large collections should not require processing everything at once. *Bounded work* handles a limited portion at a time; a page of results does not limit the total number of results. Long operations declare interruption and recovery behavior with their owners. A scheduler yield does not itself require a durable checkpoint.
 
